# Homepage slide 3 on mobile (re-learned 2026-09-24 night)

**Invariant:** A 16:9 family photo in a **portrait `h-screen` + `object-cover` box cannot look like the laptop scene.** `object-position` only picks **which ~25–31% strip** is visible. It does not “fix display.”

Owner “still not correct on the phone” is this class, not a missing CMS file.

## Shipped (2026-09-25) — always cover

Homepage charcoal **image** slides (`hero-3` today): **always `object-cover`**. Option A (`max-lg:object-contain` / contain-first) was rolled back — owner still saw left/right bars locally (any window &lt; 1024, or stale contain-first). Full-bleed wins over uncropped 16:9. White-center images and slide 1 video are unchanged. Stickers / Market S banners unchanged.

## Why local still looked letterboxed (2026-09-25)

1. **Dev server hung** (~4.5 GiB Node from Sep 22) — API/home timed out; HMR/CMS gate stuck on bootstrap spinner in some tabs. Restart `npm run dev` + Ctrl+F5.
2. **Option A contain** below 1024px — DevTools docked / split window / zoom often sits under `lg`, so laptop *looks* still letterboxed.
3. **Photo wall** — left ~30% empty wall in the WebP is not CSS; cover will not invent people there.

**Re-uploading the same `Hero_Background_Slides6.webp` does not fix this.**

## Laptop still has side gaps (historical)

**Live `origin/main` may still be older contain-first** until cover-always is committed/deployed.

Two layers on laptop:

| Layer | What it is | Same-file re-upload? |
|---|---|---|
| CSS letterbox | `contain` on a wide screen | **No** — needs cover-always code **committed and deployed** |
| Empty wall in the WebP | Left ~30% leaf shadow, people on the right | **No** — needs a **tighter crop**, not the same file |
| Charcoal HTML wash | White fog on the **viewport** left | **No** — not in the image |

After cover is actually on production, leftover “여백” next to the people is the photo composition, not missing CSS.

### Deprecated: Option A letterbox notes

Option A **did not crop**, so two kinds of “margin” showed up. They were not a broken upload.

**1. CSS letterbox (the contain box)**

`object-contain` fits the **whole** 1280×714 file inside `h-screen` without cutting.

| Viewport | Viewport AR vs photo 1.79 | Letterbox |
|---|---|---|
| Phone **portrait** (~0.46) | Photo is much **wider** | **Top and bottom** (cream gradient behind). Photo still **touches left and right** of the screen |
| Phone **landscape** or wide window still &lt; 1024 | Viewport **wider** than 1.79 | **Left and right** true CSS bars |
| Laptop with cover | `object-cover` | **No** contain bars |

On a typical upright phone under Option A, CSS did **not** add left/right bars. A short landscape band sat in the middle of the tall hero.

**2. Empty space **inside** the photo (looks like side margins)**

The file’s left ~30% is the leaf-shadow **wall** (no people). Mum/child sit center-right. `contain` showed the full frame, so the wall read as “여백”. Charcoal white wash (`from-white/78` on the **viewport** left) made the left feel even more empty.

Cousins: slide 1 video already letterboxes; charcoal wash is HTML, not baked into the WebP.

## What the phone is actually running

| Layer | Reality |
|---|---|
| Live production (`2b16cc2`) | Slide 3 charcoal + **`object-contain` then `lg:object-cover`**. Landscape laptops can still letterbox **left/right** |
| Local uncommitted | Cover by default; `max-lg:object-contain` phones only |
| CMS file | `Hero_Background_Slides6.webp` **1280×714** |

Same Swiper: **slide 1 video is `object-contain`** (whole frame). **Slide 3 image is `object-cover`** (fill + crop). That is why slide 1 feels “complete” and slide 3 feels “wrong” on the same phone.

`HeroCoverImage` `maxWidth: 1080` does **not** crop Supabase WebP (pass-through). Crop is CSS only.

## Crop math (cover, image AR 1.79, phone ~0.46)

Visible width ≈ **26%** of the file.

| `object-position` | Visible slice | What you see |
|---|---|---|
| `left` (production) | 0–26% | Leaf-shadow **wall only** |
| `center` | ~37–63% | Window / plant / sofa edge |
| `80%` (local patch) | ~59–85% | **Child + most of mum** (close-up) |
| `right` | 74–100% | Mum, may clip child |

Laptop ~16:9 ≈ image AR → almost the **full** photo. No `object-position` makes the phone equal that.

Charcoal HTML wash still sits on the **left of the viewport**, not on the left of the photo. After 80%, wash sits on the child/mum, not the wall.

## What “correct on mobile” actually requires (pick one)

Do **not** keep iterating `object-left` vs `80%` as if that equals laptop.

| Option | Effect | Cost |
|---|---|---|
| **A. `object-contain` on charcoal image slides** (same as slide 1 video) | Whole photo visible; letterbox / fallback shows at sides or top | Does not fill the screen; slide 1 already does this |
| **B. Portrait second asset** (`srcMobile`) | Art-direct faces + left negative space in a 9:19 crop | Owner uploads; code field |
| **C. Shorter mobile hero** (Market S 300–420px) | Landscape photo almost fully visible | **All three** Swiper slides share `h-screen` — would shrink slide 1 video. Homepage protection: do not do this without owner OK |
| **D. Keep cover + 80%** | Face close-up, charcoal on people | Not the laptop scene. Ship only if owner accepts a different mobile crop |

## Cousins

- Stickers / Market S **banners** are short landscape boxes — they can show most of a 16:9 file. Homepage slide 3 is **not** that box
- iPad portrait width **&lt; 1024** uses the same cover strip (not `lg:object-center`)
- iOS `h-screen` = `100vh` (taller than visible), extra vertical crop
- Sticky header overlaps the top of the strip
- Slide 2 is 1:1 — cover is worse than slide 3
- Swiper bootstrap (before chunk load) renders **slide 1 only** — not a slide-3 crop bug
- Admin Hero preview is `bg-center` in a small tile — not a phone crop
- Checking **localhost** vs **selpic.com.au**: CMS image can be live while crop CSS is not deployed

## Do not

- Treat another `object-position` tweak as “now it matches laptop”
- Blame the WebP upload or header logo
- Lower all homepage Swiper slides to a banner without owner OK (slide 1 video protected)
- Expect charcoal-left **wall** and **child** in the same portrait cover window of this file
